WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:37.220
After summer, Autumn entered into
Prince Edward Island eagerly.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:43.430
Matthew and Jerry Buote are busy
harvesting the potatoes that they planted.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:48.450
And the apple trees in the orchard
are full of bright fruits.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:55.850
Anne is working hard at her housework,
and studies every day.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:01.590
And it has been a week since
Anne stopped going to school.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:06.690
Just as Marilla was worried about, Anne
showed no interest in returning to school.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.890
She hates her Teacher
Phillips and Gilbert Blythe.

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:20.380
As much as she hated Gilbert,
however, did she love Diana,

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.650
with all the love of her
passionate little heart.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:24.010
Whatever's the matter now?

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.710
It's about Diana.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.890
What's wrong with Diana?

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.280
I love Diana so, Marilla.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.860
I cannot ever live without her.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:43.440
But I know very well when we grow up that
Diana will get married and go away.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:45.680
What shall...

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.660
What shall I do?

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.240
I hate her husband!
I just hate him furiously!

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:57.210
I've been imagining it all out.
The wedding and everything.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:03.980
Diana dressed in snowy garments,
with a veil,

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:07.990
and looking as beautiful and regal as a queen.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:13.490
And me the bridesmaid, with a lovely
dress too, and puffed sleeves,

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:17.020
but with a breaking heart
hid beneath my smiling face.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:20.260
And then bidding Diana goodbye!

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.030
Well, Anne,

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:55.750
if you must borrow trouble, for pity's
sake borrow it handier home.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:05:00.940
I should think you had an
imagination, sure enough.

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:03.880
And have you done your revisions?

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.920
Then let's begin today's cooking lesson.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:08.770
Today...

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:13.460
Even with sadness in my heart,
I must learn to cook.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.410
How realistic.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:20.270
Really... I wanted to use the
chocolate Rachel gave me

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.040
to teach you to make a chocolate cake.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:25.650
And don't forget,

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:30.330
no matter how you imagine, you
can't really eat a sweet with it.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.530
I'll learn how to do it.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:38.810
We'll start right now.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.220
That firewood is enough.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.700
The ingredients are ready so
come over here.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.530
Mix the eggs and the maple syrup
into the bowl.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:05.040
You don't have to think of anything else,
just concentrate and do it.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:26.740
That won't be enough.
Add more.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.130
That's enough!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.230
No, no! You have to beat harder!

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.560
Do it faster.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:48.710
Let me do it.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:06.330
Now you try.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:06.890
Yes!

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:13.200
Very well.
You're doing much better now.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.390
Come on, don't look elsewhere!

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:54.290
Flatten the surface.

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:01.250
Right. If it isn't flat, it would look terrible later.

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:07.820
Will this do, Marilla?

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:13.190
Now, put it into the oven,
and then tidy up these tools.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:13.880
Yes.

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:16.950
Marilla...

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.500
This is what happens if
you don't follow accordingly.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:21.510
Yes...

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:38.080
Thirty minutes. And you should never peep.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.530
Welcome back, Matthew!

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:49.800
What a nice aroma.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:52.820
There will be a chocolate cake baked by
Anne for the afternoon tea.

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:57.080
Don't worry about the taste.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:01.080
This was overseen by the
famous chef Marilla Cuthbert.

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:05.250
Well now, I was not worried.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:07.170
It must be delicious.

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:10.730
And I put my best into it.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.140
No matter what, I won't regret it.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:18.160
Really, In the kitchen, the only
thing that matters is the result.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.380
Well, come here, Anne.

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:20.050
Yes.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.860
I was thinking, if this
was an enchanted stove,

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:29.850
that whatever enters into it
would emerge tasty, I wouldn't be happy.

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:33.840
Because I wouldn't know how
my cakes really turned out...

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:34.760
Anne!

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:39.740
If you're done talking, I think the
cake in the oven is almost burnt black,

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:42.100
and your dream wouldn't come true.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.120
It should be all right, but check with this.

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:54.510
Stick it deep.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.030
All right.

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:02.600
Matthew.

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:08.300
It does look fine.

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:10.180
Smells good.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:11.950
I made it.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:14.230
It will be all right, Madam?

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:16.800
How rude, of course it will be all right.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.120
Right, Marilla?

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:20.860
If you don't taste it, I wouldn't be too sure.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:33.640
Please.

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:37.560
Here.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:39.780
Please.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:41.780
Looks delicious.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.380
Please everyone try it.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:46.760
I'll help myself then.

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:11.550
Although it's a little dry,
it's the first time you do it,

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:12.780
so I'll give you a seventy.

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:13.770
That's great!

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.380
Madam, it should be a ninety.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:17.490
Don't spout all that nonsense.

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:19.670
I mean it.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:20.920
Thank you!

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:22.450
And you, Matthew?

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.640
Well now, one hun...

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.820
Can I eat another one?

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:54.790
I made it.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.140
Of course Marilla
was helping by my side.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:59.230
It looks delicious.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.990
Marilla gave it a seventy,
and Jerry a ninety.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:07.580
Matthew said nothing,
but it should be one hundred.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:10.260
I give seventy-five.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:11.180
Why you...

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:12.490
I was joking!

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:17.130
Anne, I feel so tragic.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:22.870
I had to sit with Gertie Pye.

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:28.780
Gertie squeaks her pencil and
it makes my blood run cold.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:33.020
Ruby Gillis charmed all her warts away
with a magic pebble.

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.040
I didn't believe this at first,

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:37.080
but at the time of the new moon,

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:40.500
she rubbed the warts with the pebble and
then throw it away over her left shoulder

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.540
and the warts disapeared!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:49.330
Charlie Sloane's name was written up
with Em White's on the porch wall

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:51.920
and charlie and Em were AWFULLY MAD about it.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:56.840
But I think that Em didn't really
cared much about it.

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:01.050
Sam Boulter had "sassed" Mr. Phillips in
class and Mr. Phillips whipped him

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:04.210
and Sam's father came
down to the school and

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:08.280
dared Mr. Phillips to lay a hand
on one of his children again.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:10.700
And Gilbert Blythe...

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:12.840
I don't want to hear about him!

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:20.540
Everyone is worried about you and
hopes that you'll come back to school soon.

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:23.710
I'm happy, to know they are worried about me.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:27.350
But I am never going back to school.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:32.300
I'm sorry, Diana, for making you worry.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:35.480
It can't be helped.

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:42.110
I may not go to school, but if I can still
meet and play with you here, its enough.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.840
I'm really sorry about
what I said the other day.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:41.750
I didn't mean to offend you.

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:46.270
I didn't know you would skip
school because of that.

00:15:01.090 --> 00:15:04.060
Anne, couldn't you at least give Gil a reply?

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:06.200
You know how determined I am, don't you?

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:09.160
But I've never seen Gilbert like that.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:11.970
I think he really means to apologize.

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:15.860
I do not wish to speak with
Gilbert Blythe, or meet him either!

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:18.970
You are really strange.

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:21.310
Yes, I am really strange!

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:23.890
But, Diana, I...

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:27.590
I hope you can understand my feelings!

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:49.660
Anne, how different are you
from chickens in the way you eat?

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:55.280
I'm really sorry about
what I said the other day.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:56.300
I didn't know you would...

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:57.300
He didn't know?

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:08.640
Anne, we can still use this pudding sauce
one more time so put it on the pantry shelf.

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:09.980
Cover it well.

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:15.550
Carrots! Carrots!

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:17.440
Carrots!

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:24.760
Unforgivable!

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:26.610
Did you hear me, Anne?

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:28.900
Put the pudding sauce on the shelf.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:29.480
Yes!

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:34.160
Cover it well.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:34.920
All right!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:41.480
Carrots.

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:44.190
So what?
You're just a little bit more handsome.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:33.350
Cover it well.

00:17:57.570 --> 00:18:00.040
This happened because I was careless.

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:47.670
It should be alright now.

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:52.240
But is that sauce still edible?

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:55.130
It should be all right for the pigs.
I'll have to ask Marilla.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:03.070
It's already Autumn.

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:35.990
How beautiful it is!

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:39.190
Why do they turn into
such a beautiful colour?

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:44.410
I don't believe it's just
because of a season change.

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:46.820
That's right!
The frost fairies must have done it.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:52.740
Without they, there couldn't
be such a lovely yellow and red.

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:24.470
Anne.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:27.180
Good morning, Marilla.

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:29.150
What are you doing here
in your sleeping clothes?

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:33.590
Look. The leaves have changed colour.
Aren't they just lovely?

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:36.180
Yes. It's already autumn.

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:37.450
That's right!

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:41.740
The frost fairies changed them to this color!

00:20:42.540 --> 00:20:45.630
Really, it would be troublesome
to have snow so early.

00:20:45.630 --> 00:20:47.920
We would lose all our harvest.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:51.580
That's why the frost fairies can't be seen.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:56.920
Anne completely forgot about
the pudding sauce.

00:20:57.580 --> 00:21:01.590
And then, while Anne was
picking apples for Marilla,

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:06.340
Mr. and Mrs. Chester Ross from
Spencervale visited Green Gables.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:12.110
Marilla had to prepare something fast,
because she wasn't expecting visitors.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.780
At afternoon, Anne greeted the guests,

00:21:14.780 --> 00:21:19.360
and she was determined to be a polite
girl, since she wasn't very pretty,

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:25.450
and she wanted Mrs. Chester Ross to
think she was a ladylike little girl.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:30.650
And, when the afternoon
was about to end...

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:33.700
No. That can't be possible.

00:21:34.070 --> 00:21:35.230
Right, Matthew?

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:44.110
Please, feel free to use
as much sauce as you want.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:51.270
Marilla, you mustn't use that pudding sauce!

00:21:51.270 --> 00:21:54.050
There was a mouse drowned in it.

00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:55.910
I forgot to tell you before.

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:17.870
Well... This is...

00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:33.140
Mrs. Chester Ross is such
a perfect housekeeper,

00:22:33.150 --> 00:22:38.530
that's why I felt disgraced when I though
of what she must have thought of us.

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:42.690
Marilla turned red as fire but
she never said a word,

00:22:42.690 --> 00:22:45.510
and served strawberry preserves instead.

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:50.740
She even offered me some, but
I couldn't swallow a mouthful.

00:22:50.740 --> 00:22:54.970
It was like heaping coals of fire on my head.

00:23:06.090 --> 00:23:11.710
Of course after Mrs. Chester Ross went
away, Marilla gave me a dreadful scolding.

00:23:11.710 --> 00:23:16.480
But, Diana, I will never forget the
moment  when I saw that bottle

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:19.940
even after a million lives.

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:25.050
But why did you forget to
cover the pudding sauce?

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:30.840
I... was imagining I was a nun.

00:23:30.940 --> 00:23:33.170
Of course I'm a Protestant but

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:34.910
I imagined I was a Catholic

00:23:34.910 --> 00:23:38.540
taking the veil to bury a broken heart,
don't you think it's romantic?

00:23:39.870 --> 00:23:41.370
That's just like you.

00:23:43.220 --> 00:23:48.120
This place will be all red soon,
and also all the country.

00:23:48.760 --> 00:23:50.810
Autumn is so romantic.

00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:51.820
Yes.

00:23:54.180 --> 00:23:59.200
Anne had forgotten to cover the bottle
because was thinking about Gilbert Blythe,

00:23:59.200 --> 00:24:03.280
but she couldn't tell the truth
even to her best friend, Diana.

00:24:18.790 --> 00:24:25.360
While Anne was telling a sad story,
Diana drank many cups of raspberry cordial.

00:24:25.570 --> 00:24:28.060
Next of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:28.060 --> 00:24:30.570
Diana Is Invited to Tea with Tragic Results

00:24:30.570 --> 00:24:31.570
Please watch.
